          "text": "Toenail appearance and involvement"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Great toenails opaque yellow and thickened, with distal crumbling and onycholysis involving approximately 40–50% on the right and 30–40% on the left; some second toes also involved."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
